<section id="help-move" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-move-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-move-title">Receive and release stock</h2>
<ol><li>In <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/movements')) ?>">Stock movements</a>, find and select a product.</li><li>Choose IN to receive or OUT to release, a reason and a positive whole quantity. Add a reference or source/recipient only when useful; avoid unnecessary personal information.</li><li>Review available stock, requested quantity and expected balance, then confirm.</li></ol>
<p class="guide-note">The preview does not reserve stock; availability is checked again when saving. If a response is uncertain, retry unchanged in the same form. If you closed it, check History with an Admin before recreating the operation.</p></section>
<section id="help-corrections" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-corrections-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-corrections-title">Returns, damage and reversals</h2>
<ul><li><strong>Customer return:</strong> receive usable stock with an ordinary IN.</li><li><strong>Supplier return or damage/write-off:</strong> remove usable stock with an ordinary OUT.</li><li><strong>Recording mistake:</strong> ask an Admin to review a reversal in <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/history')) ?>">History</a>. Returns are not reversals.</li></ul>
<?php if($admin): ?><details><summary>Correct a recorded mistake</summary><ol><li>Select an unreversed original in History and enter a reason.</li><li>Review the full opposite movement at the original quantity and captured price, then confirm.</li><li>Record any corrected new movement separately.</li></ol><p>Insufficient stock, archived products and repeat reversals are refused. History is never deleted.</p></details><?php endif; ?></section>
<section id="help-units" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-units-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-units-title">Units and movement analytics</h2>
<ol><li>Check the product's base unit before entering a whole quantity; no fractions or conversions are applied.</li><li>Open <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/analytics')) ?>">Movement analytics</a>, choose a view and date shortcut or inclusive Manila dates, then Apply filters.</li><li>Read quantities by captured unit. Use the calculation disclosure for exclusions and reversal examples.</li></ol>
<p class="guide-note">Openings and physical-count adjustments are excluded. Reversals offset their original direction on the reversal date. Categories use current assignment. Ambiguous historical receipts remain excluded and visibly flagged; rankings may be incomplete. Historical units stay Unspecified when not recorded.</p>
<?php if($admin): ?><details><summary>Classify an unspecified product</summary><p>Use Product Details to establish its integer base unit explicitly. Established units cannot be casually changed; classification does not relabel old movements.</p></details><?php endif; ?></section>
<section id="help-counts" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-counts-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-counts-title">Physical stock counts</h2>
<ol><li>Open <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/stock-counts')) ?>">Physical counts</a> and choose New count.</li><li>Find a product, enter the physically counted whole quantity and give a reason for any discrepancy. Save each line.</li><li>Submit for review. Only Admin approves all adjustments together; zero discrepancies create no movement.</li></ol>
<p class="guide-note"><strong>Stale count:</strong> changed stock or eligibility blocks approval, even if stock returns to its old balance. Return to draft, physically recount and select the explicit recount option to capture a new baseline. Editing the quantity alone does not refresh it.</p>
<details><summary>Retries and completed counts</summary><p>Retry an uncertain approval unchanged in the same form. Draft/submitted counts can be cancelled. Approved/cancelled counts are historical and cannot be reopened; approved adjustments remain linked in History.</p></details></section>
<section id="help-reports" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-reports-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-reports-title">Reports and exports</h2>
<ol><li>Open <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/reports/inventory')) ?>">Inventory report</a> or <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/reports/transactions')) ?>">Transaction report</a>.</li><li>Apply filters before choosing CSV, Detailed JSON or Print this page.</li><li>Use the shown period and snapshot to understand the result.</li></ol>
<details><summary>Export scope and historical values</summary><p>CSV includes all matching rows, up to 10,000 rows / 16 MiB, using a new snapshot. Detailed JSON includes filter, snapshot and unit context. Print includes the current paginated page.</p><p>History retains archived products and inactive actors. Labels reflect current metadata; quantities, prices and times are captured history. Reference movement values are not revenue, profit or accounting valuation.</p></details></section>
<?php endif; ?>
<section id="help-account" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-account-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-account-title">Your account and recovery</h2>
<ol><li>Open <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/account')) ?>">Your account</a> to update your display name/photo, change your password or sign out.</li><li>Contact your Admin for a forgotten password or a username, role or status change. Keep the support reference from any error.</li></ol><p class="guide-note">Your own name change keeps sessions; a password change signs out other sessions. There is no public signup or password bypass.</p></section>
<?php if($admin): ?><section id="help-admin" class="panel guide-section" aria-labelledby="help-admin-title" tabindex="-1"><h2 id="help-admin-title">Account and administrative tasks</h2>
<ol><li>Maintain Categories and Suppliers before <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/products/new')) ?>">adding a product</a>. Opening stock creates a real IN; edit metadata, never the balance.</li><li>Manage access in <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/users')) ?>">Users</a>. Share temporary passwords privately; first sign-in requires a change.</li><li>Review administrative changes in <a href="<?= Ui::escape($config->url('/audit-events')) ?>">Audit log</a>, and stock changes in History.</li></ol>
<p class="guide-note">Every saved Users edit, including name-only edits, revokes existing sessions. Deactivation preserves history. The last active Admin cannot be demoted or deactivated.</p>
<details><summary>Safe edits and catalogue restrictions</summary><p>Conflicting account/category/supplier edits keep ordinary entries for reload/review. Last successful sign-in is shown in Manila time, or Not recorded. SKU cannot change after movements exist. Archive only at zero; restore retains identity/history. Referenced categories/suppliers cannot be deleted, including archived references.</p></details></section><?php endif; ?>
